        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><strong>Omar Uses Equations</strong></p><p>",
            "I wrote the equation, </p><p><em>C</em><sub><em>manager </em></sub>= 0.15<em>t </em>+ 2.50 for the cost that the manager charges. For the owner&#x27;s suggestion, I wrote the equation </p><p><em>C</em><sub><em>owner</em></sub>= 0.25<em>t</em></p><p> where <em>t </em> is the number of minutes. Then I set the two expressions for cost equal.</p><p>",
            "0.25<em>t </em> = 0.15<em>t </em>+ 2.50</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "TILETedtTHIitJxu",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<h3>Situation B. River Fun Boat Rides</h3><p>River Fun Boats (RFB) also rents canoes. The equation </p><p><em>c</em><sub><em>RFB</em></sub> = 4 + 0.10<em>t</em></p><p> gives the charge in dollars <em>c  </em>for renting a canoe for <em>t </em> minutes.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "TILEMvVVZdFPF4qf",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>1. What is the charge to rent a canoe for 20 minutes?</p><p>2. A customer at River Fun is charged $9. How long did the customer use a canoe?</p><p>3. Suppose you want to spend at most $12. How long could you use a canoe?4. How does the cost to rent a boat from River Fun Boat Rides compare to the cost to rent canoes from Sandy’s Boat House?</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "TILE9XK47fTfMr0m",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<h3>Situation C. Solving Equations- Which Strategy?</h3><p><strong>Serena Uses Tables</strong></p>"
